<h1 class="whs3"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">Display Grid</span></b></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs4">
<p class="whs5"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">This command is accessible from</font></span> <b><i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>View &gt; Display Grid</b></span></i></b> <span lang="EN-US">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>G</b></span></b><span lang="EN-US">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span lang="EN-US">Call</span> <span class="Command">Display Grid</span> <span lang="EN-US">to show grid lines in views that are orthogonal to the global co-ordinate system.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">It is applicable to all active windows. When this mode is enabled the command is marked with a tick. Call</font></span> <span class="Command">Display Grid</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">again to disable it. The state of Display Grid is not stored so next time when you run KUBE , the command will be disabled. The grid disappear if you rotate the viewport in a way making it non-orthogonal to the global co-ordinate system. Thus the grid is visible only in the predefined views (with the exception of Isometric).</font></span></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial; text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165610619" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Images/image19.gif" width="620px" height="454px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="whs5"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Grid lines are divided in major and minor lines. There are numerous of grid settings located in <u><a href="Display_Settings_-_Grid.htm">Preferences / Display / Grid</a></u> dialog. It is possible to change the spacing (in mm) and width (in pixels) of the minor lines, the number of minor lines per major line, and the width (in pixels) of major lines. It is also possible to add values of the major and/or minor lines. Grid colours appear in the colour schemes.</font></span></p>
<p class="Use" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use:</b></span> <span class="Command">Display Grid</span> <span lang="EN-US">is useful for quick measurement of object extensions.</span></p>
<p class="whs5"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;"><a href="javascript:void(0);" onclick="var e; if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion)&gt;=4){e=event;} if (parseInt(navigator.appVersion) &gt;=2 &amp;&amp; typeof(PopupMenu_Invoke) == 'function') PopupMenu_Invoke(e,'','Back','back.htm','Down','down.htm','Front','front.htm','Left','Left.htm','Preferences - Display - Grid','Display_Settings_-_Grid.htm','Right','Right.htm','Up','Up.htm');return false;" title=""><img src="../add_on/ss_btn_see_also.gif" border="0" height="17" width="60" alt=""></a></font></span></p>
